 answer in time, the step fails with `ACTION_FAILED` and isn't retried: the
-input may have landed. A `longPress` that holds at least as long as the
+input may have landed. Press requests are cancelled when the adapter stops
+waiting, including its minimum 250 ms acknowledgement allowance, or on interruption.
+This stops native readiness polling for an input that has not dispatched.
+A `longPress` that holds at least as long as the
 time left is refused before it's sent; raise its `timeout`. Snapshots and
 screenshots run within the timeout of the call that takes them, so a device
 that stops answering fails the step with `ACTION_FAILED` instead of holding
